Subject: [PATCH] Delete unused fresh render targets early while the texture cache is over budget

Port of PS5_Lichii 0227 (mihawk-99 70b85df4), itself Fritchii#34 / Lichii#1023 (Ghostwolf13),
onto T85. Replaces an earlier draft of this number that only took fully cleared colour targets
and walked the whole LRU each frame. EDEN_NX2_RT_EVICT_PRESSURE=<frames> turns it on (unset or
0: off, and render targets load the guest memory under them as before). Kept from the draft:
a target bound now or with a download pending is never deleted. slot_vector gains contains()
for the queue's ids. A line every 600 frames says how many targets and MiB went.

diff --git a/src/common/slot_vector.h b/src/common/slot_vector.h
--- a/src/common/slot_vector.h
+++ b/src/common/slot_vector.h
@@ -138,6 +138,15 @@
         ResetStorageBit(id.Value());
     }
 
+    /// Whether `id` names a live slot (queues that keep ids across frames check before use).
+    [[nodiscard]] bool contains(SlotId id) const noexcept {
+        if (!id) {
+            return false;
+        }
+        const u32 index = id.Value();
+        return index / 64 < stored_bitset.size() && ((stored_bitset[index / 64] >> (index % 64)) & 1) != 0;
+    }
+
     [[nodiscard]] Iterator begin() noexcept {
         const auto it = std::ranges::find_if(stored_bitset, [](u64 value) { return value != 0; });
         if (it == stored_bitset.end()) {
